    "narrative": "For LawDog\u2019s roster on 2026-07-23, **Jonathan Aranda** stands out as the premier play with a 70.47 efficiency score. His matchup against Bieber is highly favorable; the 5.10 xERA of the opposing starter, combined with **Aranda** hitting in the #2 hole and a 19% boost from the SP skill profile, makes him our primary catalyst today. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a core anchor at 65.73. While his SP Skill adjustment is slightly negative against Bradley, his elite standing in the lineup and a 2% boost from a slow-delivery pitcher\u2014which keeps our aggressive stolen base targets in play\u2014solidify his high floor. **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Gleyber Torres** occupy a \"strong\" tier, with both benefiting from top-of-the-order assignments, though **Gleyber Torres** faces a minor dip due to platoon splits against a right-handed starter.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins was benching **Gavin Sheets**, who finished with a 35.12 score. While his base projection is competent, the combination of facing an elite arm like Sale (which depressed his score by 19%) and his platoon disadvantage as a left-handed hitter against a lefty starter rendered him \"Below Floor.\" Consequently, he sits to preserve game caps, ceding opportunity to the rest of the infield. **Masyn Winn** rounds out the starters with a 53.61 score; while his power profile is modest, the 86% stolen base efficiency against the opposing pitcher\u2019s delivery ensures he remains a necessary asset in our effort to win the scarce SB category. \n\nWe are monitoring no severe weather risks, though we continue to track the health of **Will Smith**, who remains on the IL, alongside our other bench stalwarts like **Cal Raleigh** and **Bryce Harper**, who are off today. **Ryan Waldschmidt** is active in the outfield despite a lower score (47.61), as his utility remains high even with the negative park adjustments. We will continue to evaluate the performance of **Lawrence Butler**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Taylor Ward**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Matt Chapman**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Zack Gelof**, **Luis Arraez**, **Brendan Donovan**, **JJ Bleday**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Drew Gilbert** as the 2026 stretch run intensifies, ensuring our cap management remains aligned with ATC projections.",
